    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mo>[</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>]</mo><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>R</mi></math> be defined as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></math>&nbsp;for all <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mo>[</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>]</mo><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>R</mi></math> such that&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;and for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math> the maximum value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>&#34;</mo></msup><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>.</mo></math> If&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;then the least value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math> is equal to",
